CORE
main.cpp
--cpp11
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ the more specialized template: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
^CONVERSION ERROR$
--
Partial ordering compared parameter-type-lists of equal length only, so
the call was ambiguous between invoke(Args&&...) and invoke(F&&, Args&&...)
(also on develop).  libc++ 19's std::__invoke has this pair; every
ranges algorithm with a projection reached it (__get_property and
__estimated_width in <format>, std::apply: the macOS CI job).
